x724 text "editing"
x725 puts x723 x724
x726 call open x725 11
x727 write x726 2
x728 text "Views and edits"
x729 puts x727 x728
x730 call close x729 
x731 call open x730 2
x732 write x731 2
x733 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0) and, when the whole program matters, a program handle (g0) with one signature line per function. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line: `id op ...` replaces the instruction id or inserts it before ret; `id op ... @ other` inserts after other; `-id` deletes; `ret x` changes the result. Under g0, a whole `fn ... end` block adds or replaces a function and `-fn name` removes one. The edit is applied only if it parses, type-checks, validates, and was written against the current revision; otherwise it is rejected and the handle stays valid."
x734 puts x732 x733
x735 call close x734 
x736 call open x735 10
x737 write x736 4
x738 write x737 2
